<v Justin>This may sound terrible, but it probably was a result of how nurturing she is. She doesn't even like to step on spiders, you know what I'm saying? So I just never thought that that would be an option for her.
<v Justin>这听起来可能很糟糕，但这大概是因为她太有爱心了。她甚至连踩死一只蜘蛛都不忍心，你知道我的意思吗？所以我从没想到过这对她来说会是一个选择。

00:38:58.720 --> 00:39:20.920
<v Caroline Kitchener>But Justin quickly moved past shock and into action mode. He assumed that this was something that he needed to make happen for his daughter. The day Lilly told him she wanted an abortion, Justin went to work and researched. He looked up clinics. He had no idea that Lilly, his baby-- now his anxious and somewhat irresponsible teenager-- she was way ahead of him.
<v Caroline Kitchener>但贾斯汀很快从震惊转向了行动模式。他认为这是他需要为女儿去做的事情。在莉莉告诉他她想要堕胎的那天，贾斯汀去工作并进行了研究。他查了诊所。他根本没想到莉莉——他的小宝贝，那个焦虑又有点不负责任的十几岁女孩，已经走在他前面了。

00:39:20.920 --> 00:39:44.890
<v Justin>Didn't really hear from her much that day. And I get home, fully, she's laying on her bed. She's got her little notebook out. And she's got some kind of gangster rap going on the freaking-- on the Alexa. And she's called 14 different places. She's called the Roe v. Wade fund. She's called everything, and she's basically got a plan in place. And I'm like, oh, wow.
