<v Justin>I did. I absolutely did. It amazed me because that is not a trait she had displayed before. And her calmness during it, that's what really stood out. She didn't panic. She wasn't like, oh, Dad, help me. She was like, OK, well, I got to call this guy. I got to call this guy.
<v Justin>我是这么想的。绝对是的。这让我感到惊奇，因为这是她以前从没表现出来的特质。她在过程中的冷静，那才是真正让我印象深刻的。她没有恐慌。她没有说，噢，爸爸，帮帮我。她只是说，好吧，我要打电话给这个人。我要打电话给那个人。

00:40:03.800 --> 00:40:12.130
<v Caroline Kitchener>What did you want her to do? What decision did you want her to make?
<v Caroline Kitchener>你想要她怎么做？你希望她做出什么决定？

